{"id": "section-body-11181", "title": "Deep Vein Thrombosis in Pregnancy", "chapterId": "chapter-eleven", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "OBSTETRICS, GYNECOLOGY AND CONTRACEPTION", "Antenatal Care", "Deep Vein Thrombosis in Pregnancy"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-11181", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Deep Vein Thrombosis in Pregnancy", "runs": [{"text": "Deep"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Vein"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Thrombosis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pregnancy"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1452"}}, {"id": "body-11182", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Deep vein thrombosis (DVT) and acute pulmonary embolism (PE) are two manifestations of venous thromboembolism (VTE. The risk of VTE is increased in pregnancy by about five times because of a more hyper-coagulable state. VTE contributes to significant maternal morbidity and mortality. The mainstay of therapy for DVT is anticoagulation, provided there is no contraindication.", "runs": [{"text": "Deep vein thrombosis (DVT) and acute pulmonary embolism (PE) are two manifestations of venous thromboembolism (VTE. The risk of VTE is increased in pregnancy by about five times because of a more hyper-coagulable state. VTE contributes to significant maternal morbidity and mortality. The mainstay of therapy for DVT is anticoagulation, provided there is no "}, {"text": "contraindication."}]}, {"id": "body-11184", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-11185", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Pain on the affected limb", "runs": [{"text": "Pain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "affected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "limb"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1427"}}, {"id": "body-1118